MIST isochrones in SDSS ugriz
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
js/data/observations/mistSdssIsochrones.js
Derived from the MIST v1.2 isochrones with SDSS ugriz synthetic photometry
(MIST_v1.2_vvcrit0.0_SDSSugriz.txz): https://mist.science/

As with the MIST tracks above, MIST asks that its papers be cited and states
no separate redistribution license. What is bundled is a thinned subset for
teaching - three metallicities, seven ages, the main-sequence, giant-branch
and core-helium-burning phases, each curve simplified to 0.005 mag - with the
archive's size and SHA-256 and every reduction recorded in
data-packs/mist-sdss-isochrones.json.

  Dotter (2016), ApJS 222, 8, doi:10.3847/0067-0049/222/1/8
  Choi et al. (2016), ApJ 823, 102, doi:10.3847/0004-637X/823/2/102
  Paxton et al. (2011), ApJS 192, 3, doi:10.1088/0067-0049/192/1/3
  Paxton et al. (2013), ApJS 208, 4, doi:10.1088/0067-0049/208/1/4
