===============================================================================
Planetary states from JPL Horizons (DE441)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
js/data/ephemeris/solarSystem2025.js, js/data/ephemeris/solarSystem2025Check.js
Derived from heliocentric states of Venus, the Earth, Mars and the Jupiter
system barycenter, 2025 to 2045, served by the NASA/JPL Horizons system of the
Solar System Dynamics group: https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/horizons/

Horizons states no license for its output and asks that the Solar System
Dynamics group and the ephemeris be credited. What is bundled is a reduced
derivative for teaching - Chebyshev coefficients fitted to daily states, and a
set of held-out states to check them - with every request and the SHA-256 of
every answer's data rows recorded in ephemeris-packs/solar-system-2025-2045.json.
`npm run ephemeris:provenance` rebuilds the pack from those answers.

  Park, Folkner, Williams and Boggs (2021), AJ 161, 105,
  doi:10.3847/1538-3881/abd414 - the DE440 and DE441 ephemerides

